TODO: custom voi.ci names (feat/named-links) and the branches stacked on it
===========================================================================

For the review engineer. This file lists everything that is unproven or still
needs a person, for the work built in this session. Read it first, work down
it, and DELETE THIS FILE when every item is done or moved (last line).

What was built
--------------
Branch order (each branch sits on the one before; all pushed, all current with
feat/multilingual @ 9624e1c36 as of 2026-10-23):

  main -> feat/multilingual -> feat/named-links -> feat/marketplace
       -> feat/custom-domains / feat/custom-names / feat/outbound-proxy

Webapp shell versions: named-links v159, marketplace v160, custom-domains v161,
custom-names v162, outbound-proxy v163. The plan and rules are in
docs/named-links.md; the status entry is in AGENTS.md ("Custom voi.ci names").

How to work through this
------------------------
- Work in a worktree with its own node_modules (npm ci), never a symlinked one.
- Per branch, the gate is: npx tsc -b; npm run i18n; npm run parity (expect the
  9 old "anchor broke" reds, no new ones); then vitest on apps/web/tests,
  apps/com, packages/control-plane, packages/storage, packages/server-daemon.
  Do NOT run the whole tools/ or scripts/ test trees unscoped in the cloud
  container: one run of them deleted the checkout (cause not found).
- Rebase order matters (bottom up). A rebase onto a moved parent conflicts in
  generated i18n files and in the shell-version pins; settle the source
  catalogs (i18n/<surface>/*.json) by union, take upstream for generated
  output, then rebuild with scripts/i18n-<surface>.mjs build.

A. Unproven: nothing below has run on a device or a live system
---------------------------------------------------------------
A1. iOS code (feat/named-links): nothing was compiled. Build the app from
    apps/mobile/ios/App/FlagshipApp.xcodeproj. Likely fixes: confirmationDialog
    with presenting:, onChange closures, @Observable with nonisolated static
    members, Keystore / BiometricGate use in VoiciLinkViewModel.swift and
    VoiciLinkField.swift. Run the new tests: VoiciLinkViewModelTests,
    VoiciNameVectorTests (shared vectors: packages/protocol/test-vectors/voici-name).
A2. iOS strings: run `node scripts/i18n-ios.mjs harvest` on a Mac (new
    String(localized:) keys; removed short-link strings), then build/check.
    The marketplace, custom-domains and outbound-proxy Swift text was never
    harvested at all.
A3. Android code: nothing was compiled or unit-tested (no SDK in the cloud).
    Build and run the tests: LinkFieldViewModelTest, VoiciNameVectorsTest,
    NameDibsViewModelTest, AuditLogViewModelTest, and the tests of the
    outbound-proxy and marketplace screens (some may compare old English
    strings now served from resources). Check the new nav route
    name-dibs-link/{name} and that the field's state survives the trip to the
    dibs screen (view model key link-field-<serviceId>). Run
    scripts/release-clean-sources.test.ts and
    apps/mobile/android/scripts/check-release-clean.sh on a built APK.
A4. Gym group `named-links` (tools/live-e2e/groups/namedLinks.ts) is written
    but has never run. Run it after bash scripts/gym-refresh.sh:
      npx tsx tools/live-e2e/shared-run.ts --only named-links   (check --list)
    It may fail on a missing certificate for <app>.<user>.<gym apex> (tier-2
    cert); decide whether that is a gym gap or a real one. voi.ci is a fixed
    host, so redirects are not covered live; they are covered by
    packages/control-plane/tests/voiciNames.test.ts.
A5. Canonical address (decision 3): the box change (packages/server-daemon
    gossip/gossipLoop.ts extraSiblings, accessPeers.ts peerRunners, wired in
    index.ts) feeds .com's server list plus a direct ask of each server into
    the election, because gossip frames have never reached a sibling live.
    Unit tests pass; nothing ran on two real boxes. Prove: two boxes run an
    app, the first in the server order serves <app>.<user>.<apex>, and it moves
    when that box stops running the app (gym group above). Only then set
    VOICI_CANONICAL = "1" (apps/com/wrangler*.toml, commented note there).
    While it is off, voi.ci redirects use the stored/app URL as before.
A6. Gossip needs a CGK; without one no box claims a canonical route at all.
    Decide whether the canonical address must work without a CGK.
A7. Redirect, 410 and waiting-period behaviour are tested in control-plane
    tests only. Do one live pass on voi.ci after the .com deploy: custom name
    redirects, random code still redirects, a released name answers 410 for 30
    days, a retired code answers 410.
A8. Timing-sensitive tests: apps/com/test/cpuBudget.test.ts and cronBudget.test.ts
    fail intermittently in the cloud container (values swing, "Infinity x
    calibration"), and pass on re-run or on a quiet machine. Run them on a quiet
    machine; if cronBudget still fails for the plan "demo+suggestions+eviction-gc
    +voici-names", the voici-names job needs a smaller window (VOICI_NAMES_PER_RUN
    in apps/com/src/cronPlan.ts).
A9. Translations are machine drafts; no native reviewer has seen any of them
    (webapp, site, Android, iOS server sentences) for: Your link / Free one up /
    I own it / dibs text, the marketplace and Pro text, custom domains, outbound
    proxy. See i18n/REVIEW.md. The dibs text was generalised (no more "$20 name
    change"), check the English once more.
A10. Android accepted the freshness of ~40 keys with `accept` after the rebase
    onto multilingual (they were translated together with their English on
    this branch). Spot check a few in all six languages.

B. Left for the owner / release (deploy and config)
---------------------------------------------------
B1. D1 migrations before the .com deploy: 0107 (voici_names, voici_name_changes,
    voici_links.retired_at) on named-links. On the marketplace branch family:
    0090-0091 (marketplace), 0092-0094 (custom-names), 0099 (outbound-proxy).
    `main` skips those numbers on purpose; apply in order against the live DB.
B2. Dibs window: set DIBS_WINDOW_START and DIBS_WINDOW_END in apps/com/wrangler
    config (six months from this release; the example in wrangler.toml says
    2026-10-15 to 2027-04-15 and must be changed to the real dates). Unset means
    dibs is off and every free name is open to everyone.
B3. Endorsed box release: needed for the canonical-address election change
    (A5) and for the other box-side changes already waiting on main.
B4. iOS and Android store builds (the link field and everything above ships in
    the apps). iOS needs the harvest (A2) first.
B5. Not in this build, decide: .com has no per-service delete signal, so a
    deleted app's random code only retires with its account. A box-side signal
    would fix it. Push notifications for the 30/7-day release warnings are
    Activity events only; a content-free push needs a localized sentence.
B6. Plan limits are code constants (VOICI_NAME_LIMITS 5/25/100, 3 changes per
    30 days, 10 per day, 30-day wait, 60-day inactivity) in
    packages/control-plane/src/voiciNames.ts; confirm them before launch.
B7. The marketplace branch family still holds unlaunched features. Merge order
    when they launch: named-links first (after multilingual), then
    marketplace, then the three children. Rebase, do not merge, as above.
B8. Parity: after merging, the `named-links` row in parity/features.json has
    web/ios/android all "present"; if any port is cut, set it back to missing
    with a reason.

